WEBVTT

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.620
Huh? Wha...

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.330
What?!

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.260
What, what?! What's going on?!

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.480
What is this? Wat eez dees?

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.050
You're awake?

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:34.770
Who are you?

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.280
Shingetsu-chan?

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.850
Do you want to take a bath?

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.570
It's morning already...

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:12.050
<b>GRANBELM</b>

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:11.960
The Two Princeps

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.850
At the moment, there doesn't seem 
to be any criminal activity at play,

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.610
but if anything happens, contact us here.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:31.570
All right...

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:32.960
Thank you.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.920
Onee-chan...

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.430
This is bad! This is so, so bad!

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.890
<b>Mom 
Mom 
Mom 
Kohinata Kibou 
Mom 
Mom 
Kohinata Kibou 
Kohinata Kibou 
Mom</b>

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.010
I guess that's no surprise...

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:48.170
What's so bad?

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:50.760
We came back here last night,

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.040
but you were so deeply asleep...

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.390
You should've woken me up! 
No matter how deeply asleep I was!

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:59.360
Then again, it was the middle of 
the night, so it'd still be bad...

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:02.780
Your sister is crying.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.060
Shouldn't you hurry over there?

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:08.530
I know! If I do, everyone will be so happy!

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.570
They'll all cry and hug me!

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:13.420
But the problem is what comes after that...

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.980
It is?

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.170
What?

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:21.180
I have... a favor to ask!

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:27.300
So this girl was sick, and you fell
 asleep while looking after her?

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.060
Yep!

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:28.980
And your phone?

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.660
I had it in silent mode!

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.610
I didn't want to wake her up, you know?

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.670
Still, you could've called just once...

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:42.470
Well, it's all right. You're back now.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:44.110
I guess that's true.

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.660
I think I'll take a nap.

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:49.740
I can't believe I got away 
with an excuse like that!

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:52.520
Even I felt like that was pushing it...

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.750
I manipulated the magnetic field.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:58.880
To calm them down, I turned the yin to yang.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.880
Is that like... magic?

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.800
It's nothing fancy.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.120
But all descendants of mages 
have the simple ability

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.640
to manipulate magnetic fields,
even with no magical power.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:14.340
Like this?

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.020
That's kinda cool!

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:21.550
You really don't know anything about mages?

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:24.590
Your grandparents never 
mentioned these things to you?

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:27.030
Nope, never.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:31.800
And last night was your first time 
appearing in that space, wasn't it?

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.130
What... What?

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.510
Don't worry.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.360
I'm only replaying your memories as a video.

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:53.640
It's true... I don't sense any 
relationships to mages.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:54.780
You see?

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:57.080
But...

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:03.460
Well, normally, the only ones 
who can enter that space

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:08.100
are those who wish to fight in GRANBELM 
and undergo the ritual to do so.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.390
I've never heard of
 anyone joining mid-battle.

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:13.640
None of that means anything to me!

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.610
There must be some mistake, right?

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:17.590
Do you have your magic stone?

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:19.830
Huh? Oh...

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:21.670
This?

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:28.310
It seems very pure.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.180
Where did you get it?

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:33.530
I'm not really sure...

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.310
It's true! I really don't know!

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.490
Well, anyway, you have no 
desire to fight, correct?

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.590
Well... no...

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:50.870
And no desire to obtain that magical 
power and become the Princeps mage?

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:52.310
Not really.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:53.950
Understood.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.510
What're you doing now?

00:05:55.510 --> 00:05:58.950
I'm going to erase all memories you 
have of GRANBELM and the mages.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.410
Oh...

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:01.290
Wait, what?!

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.360
W-W-Wait!

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:05.990
Wh-What is it?

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:07.690
Why would you erase them?!

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:09.040
Well, you don't need them, do you?

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.390
No, no! That's not the issue here!

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:15.850
The ritual to enter GRANBELM is known 
only to those born into mage bloodlines.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:18.310
It's nothing you should 
involve yourself with!

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.310
Bu... Wai—

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:35.990
I see it.

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:54.780
<i>The technique didn't work...</i>

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.120
What?

00:06:58.120 --> 00:06:59.860
Just who are you?

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:04.570
I told you... I'm just what I look 
like, an ordinary high school girl.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:07.790
Oh, come on!

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:10.900
I told you I wouldn't mention this to anyone!

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.530
Just teach me already!

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.620
What will you do with the knowledge?

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:20.830
I dunno, but I have a right to hear it, don't I?

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:30.800
So, does that mean you're the 
descendant of a mage, too?

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:32.130
Yes.

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:34.590
To those of us descended from mages,

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:37.400
being a mage is our identity.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.750
Now that magical power has 
vanished from the world,

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:44.280
there's no way for anyone to become a mage

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:46.730
except to become the one
 and only Princeps mage.

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:51.020
And so, once every several decades,

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:53.290
when the moon's power is at its fullest,

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:56.330
descendants of mages from 
around the world gather

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:59.690
and perform the ritual to 
call forth Magiaconatus,

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:02.160
which signals the start of GRANBELM.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.060
Our dream is to become that lost mage.

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:11.970
You look as if you're having 
trouble believing this.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:14.720
That's because I <i>am</i> having 
trouble believing it.

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:17.190
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:20.910
Either way, it doesn't 
concern you any longer.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:25.480
Huh? But the battle won't end 
until only one remains, right?

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:28.330
You can simply refrain from participating.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:31.410
The battle is held on 
the night of the full moon.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:34.910
If you miss the ritual and 
refuse to enter that space,

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.620
you lose your right to fight.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.630
I see...

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.080
What?

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:42.510
Your magic stone.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:46.090
What're you gonna do?

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:47.310
Dispose of it.

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:51.090
What's the matter?

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:56.590
If you do that, I'll never be able to enter 
that Magia-whatever thing again, right?

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:57.750
And?

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:00.840
That robot... WHITE LILY, was it?

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.380
What'll happen to it?

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:03.730
It will disappear, of course.

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:07.180
An ARMANOX is a magical doll created

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:12.000
when the magical power filling 
Magiaconatus responds to the user's will.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.780
The same is true of my VIOLA 
KATZE and Anna's ACONITE GRIS.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.010
It's basically your body double.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:21.950
I see...

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:39.150
I ended up bringing it home.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:46.740
W-Well, there's still a month 
until the next full moon, right?

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:49.050
I'd like to give it a little more thought...

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.630
And what will you do after that?

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.090
Well, I mean...

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.430
What <i>do</i> I want to do?

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.490
Gate, close!

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:22.730
Wait! I can still keep going! I'm still—

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:23.770
Rosa.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:26.090
You understand, don't you?

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:30.350
Now that your magical power has been 
taken from you, you are worthless.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:37.470
Oh, my...

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:39.960
It's a piece of junk! Bids start at zero yen!

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.320
Shut up!

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:43.500
What do you expect to do with this?

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:51.720
Just get out of my sight,

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:53.800
loser of GRANBELM.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.300
Bye-bye!

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:09.040
Bring me a rose tea. 
As cold as you can make it.

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.610
You got it!

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.410
Ernesta...

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:29.710
Die!

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:34.330
You cannot defeat me.

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:40.050
Hot...

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:43.330
It's so hot...

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:50.130
Onee-chan really tries hard.

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:54.120
Morning!

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:55.220
What do you want?

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:58.040
Just wondering if you didn't 
get enough sleep again.

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:01.740
Shut up! Unlike brats like you,
 I have things to do at ni—

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:04.160
That hurt...

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.360
Are you okay?

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:07.230
Did I not just say it hurts?!

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:12.030
You never change, Nene-chan.

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:14.020
I swear, Nana and Mimi are both the same!

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:16.740
Can't tell if they're laid-back or just slow!

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:21.520
Nana and Mimi? The little sisters from 
Hong Kong that you mentioned before?

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:22.590
Yes!

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:23.840
Are they coming here?

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.660
They're still in Hong Kong.

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:28.750
Then maybe I'll come sleep 
over at your place sometime.

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:29.470
Why?!

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:30.680
I can't?

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:35.830
I mean... I guess I don't care.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.600
Is that fashion?

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:49.770
Just stupidity.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:59.250
<b>Japanese OK</b>

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:58.300
Oh, it's Onee-chan!

00:12:58.300 --> 00:12:59.250
Really?

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:00.810
Hello?

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.440
<i>I told you to start the process 
for getting me out of middle school!</i>

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:08.290
We can't help it. It's mandatory in Japan.

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:11.510
<i>And I've told you that I'm an adult!</i>

00:13:11.510 --> 00:13:14.070
Don't be so selfish, Nene-nee.

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:15.970
Just look in the mirror.

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:18.920
You don't look like anything 
but a middle school girl.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:23.740
<i>And I asked you two to
explain that to the school!</i>

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:23.740
We're hanging up.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:27.470
Should you have done that? 
Nene-nee will be mad.

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:30.700
It's fine. If she wants 
to argue, I won't lose.

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:33.400
Here.

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:34.750
Thanks!

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.580
I'll bring the box back when I'm done, okay?

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:37.640
Okay.

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:41.590
A technique, huh?

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:49.940
Of course...

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:52.310
What's that?

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:57.140
Okay, take your seats.

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:00.520
Before we start today, I'm 
introducing a transfer student.

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:11.340
My name is Shingetsu Ernesta Fukami.

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:13.990
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:21.080
Why didn't you tell me those 
were for grade school children?

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:23.040
Didn't I tell you that I lived in Germany

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:26.170
and only came to Japan when I was younger?!

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:30.560
Well, I never expected you 
to transfer into my school.

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:33.050
I did it because you won't make up your mind!

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:34.260
Me?

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:36.980
Wait, you did this because of me?

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:39.920
I have no guarantee that 
you won't tell anyone,

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:42.620
and I'm sure you're
 confused after all of it...

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:44.690
And...

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:46.150
And?

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:48.860
Nothing.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.100
Want some?

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:57.190
N-No, I'm really not...

00:14:57.190 --> 00:14:59.680
It's okay. I made a bunch.

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:02.230
In that case, okay...

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:02.900
Sure!

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:06.340
Have you made up your mind?

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:07.680
About what?

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:09.080
GRANBELM.

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:10.780
Oh... well...

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:11.970
Mangetsu-chan!

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:12.970
What's up?

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:16.040
Do you have an extra lunch?

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:18.580
There's one more girl saying she wants one.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.640
Oh, if you don't, it's okay!

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:24.560
Sorry about that.

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:25.970
Wait!

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:27.950
I haven't started eating this one yet.

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.540
Huh? But...

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:34.220
It's fine. I'm on a diet, anyway.

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:36.650
This must be a message from 
above to lose more weight.

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:37.290
Here.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.350
Thanks!

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.430
Decide among yourselves 
how to divide up the work.

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:44.210
You'll present your results next week.

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:46.800
You can do the presentation, Kaori-chan.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:47.770
Okay.

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:51.040
I'll buy the stuff we 
need for the experiment.

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:53.940
Who's going to collect the 
bug poop from the mountain?

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.100
We've gotta do that, too?

00:15:57.100 --> 00:16:00.020
Okay, I'll do that part.

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:01.000
Are you sure?

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:03.810
Yeah! The mountain's not far from my house.

00:16:04.050 --> 00:16:05.810
Really? Great, thanks!

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:08.320
Fujita   Kitamura   Tozaki 

00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:12.560
There, all done.

00:16:15.090 --> 00:16:16.930
You're not even on duty today.

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:20.160
The other kids aren't bullying you, are they?

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:23.420
Huh? Not at all. Everyone's really nice.

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:26.240
I just said I'd do it.

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:27.800
Why?

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:32.170
Because there's nothing 
else I can do, really.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:38.020
I'm not good at studying or sports,

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:40.630
so nothing good happens 
when I try to butt in.

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:46.390
I just hold everyone back in jumping 
rope and class relays and stuff.

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:50.200
And that's why you volunteer to do this?

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:51.720
Yeah.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:57.450
But... I kinda want someone 
to notice, you know?

00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:00.520
That I'm here, I mean.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:08.700
When you told me I might 
be the descendant of a mage

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:13.760
and was recognized as a participant 
in GRANBELM, I was really surprised.

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:19.740
I couldn't even imagine it. For me of all 
people, it just didn't seem possible.

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.170
I mean, I'm... me.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.180
Why do you feel that way?

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:29.190
Because... I don't have anything.

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:34.490
So if I have the power to 
control that weird robot

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:40.370
or to become this one and only 
Princeps mage you told me about...

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:45.590
I kind of want to go for it!

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.470
I thought you might say that.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:56.940
You weren't willing to give me your 
magic stone, so I suspected as much.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.650
Amazing...

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:11.450
Do you think so?

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:15.240
It's a simple technique that made 
these flowers bloom so beautifully.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:20.740
But in my doing so, the flowers lost the 
ability to bloom when they were meant to.

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:22.950
I disturbed their fate.

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:27.160
And magical power can't 
even be compared to this.

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:31.420
Its strength diverts things from 
the paths they were meant to follow,

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:34.450
makes what should be impossible possible,

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:37.830
and makes things that shouldn't 
exist come into being.

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:43.450
Gaining that kind of power is not 
a wonderful thing, by any means.

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:48.120
Still, it's better than having nothing.

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:51.580
There aren't any humans who have nothing.

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:53.150
That's not true.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:56.560
There isn't. That's just what 
you've made yourself believe.

00:18:56.560 --> 00:18:57.320
Every human—

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:58.320
I have nothing!

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:02.440
I seriously have nothing.

00:19:04.900 --> 00:19:08.460
It's not that everyone around me is mean.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:11.360
I'm not trying to isolate myself, either.

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:14.410
But no matter where I go,

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:17.530
it wouldn't really matter 
whether I was there or not.

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:21.250
Everyone's nice,

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:25.020
but even if I wasn't around, 
I'm sure they'd all be just fine.

00:19:25.590 --> 00:19:28.470
I sort of feel like I'm invisible.

00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:30.640
That's why...

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:36.960
That's why you'll fight.

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:41.970
That's why you say you'll 
try to become a mage?

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:43.860
When you know nothing?

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:46.470
I don't know...

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:49.060
But I have the right, don't I?

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:53.050
The ones who participate in 
GRANBELM are descendants of mages.

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:57.050
Each one wishes so strongly to become a mage 
that they would give their lives for it.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:19:59.010
I don't believe you could win.

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:18.650
One with such a pure heart 
should not strive to be a mage.

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:35.500
But still!

00:20:38.390 --> 00:20:40.960
But still, I...

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:45.500
It's pointless.

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:46.990
That's fine!

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:49.040
I'm doing something only I can do,

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:52.250
something no one else can do!

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:55.320
That's amazing to me!

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:57.400
I wouldn't trade it for anything!

00:20:57.860 --> 00:20:58.900
Mangetsu...

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:03.370
So if I give up on that from 
the start... if I let it go...

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.490
I know I'll regret it.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:09.070
I'll keep thinking about it 
until the day I die!

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:11.690
But...

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:19.900
This is...

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:54.090
Can't I...

00:21:58.220 --> 00:22:01.530
Can't I do it?

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:07.180
Hold it!

00:22:12.900 --> 00:22:15.060
Think about it.

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:19.020
That girl... Ernesta...

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:24.480
is a demon!

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:26.990
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:56.990 --> 00:24:00.000
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:02.290
<i>Shingetsu is reunited with Anna Fugo.</i>

00:24:03.190 --> 00:24:05.140
<i>One who has, and one who does not have...</i>

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:10.130
<i>Theirs is an endless, hateful 
paranoia born of anger and sadness.</i>

00:24:10.740 --> 00:24:15.470
<i>Will magical power cruelly separate 
these two lives from one another?</i>

00:24:16.570 --> 00:24:18.060
<i>Next time on </i>GRANBELM<i>,</i>

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:20.560
<b>The Bell Tolls at the Full Moon</b>

00:24:18.670 --> 00:24:20.560
<i>"The Bell Tolls at the Full Moon."</i>

00:24:21.620 --> 00:24:24.850
<i>The moon closes its eyes to the girl's wish.</i>

00:24:27.020 --> 00:24:30.030
<b>Look forward to the next episode!</b>
